  "worked_solution": "First, we carry out the substitution\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}=\\frac{{({b}^{9})}^{3}}{{b}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply power rule followed by the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{({b}^{9})}^{3}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{b}^{9\\cdot 3}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{b}^{27}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ {b}^{27-2} & = \\\\ {b}^{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
